            "value" : "1. Choose where replies will come from: select MCP for an AI on a platform that supports MCP; Backend for an existing conversation service adapted for Tincall; or Standalone to configure a model and persona in Tincall.\n\n2. Prepare that source: for Standalone, add and test a chat model in API Settings. For Backend or MCP, deploy or connect the appropriate service in Cloud Sync & Calls → Connect to Cloud and save the connection.\n\n3. Set up speech: add and test a voice preset in Text to Speech. Select a service in My Settings → Speech Recognition, enter any required credentials, and run its test.\n\n4. Create or edit a contact and select the call mode and voice preset. For Standalone, also select a chat model and enter a persona. For Backend, select the connection and conversation partner. For MCP, select the connection and save, then copy that contact’s full MCP configuration to the matching AI platform and start the AI using the integration instructions on this page.\n\nOpen the call screen, complete any missing items, and allow microphone access when first using voice input. Copying an MCP configuration does not mean the AI on the platform is already waiting."
