    "1. 先确定通话方式：要通过支持 MCP 的平台与 AI 通话，选 MCP；已有适配 Tincall 的对话后端，选后端；想在 Tincall 内配置模型和对话设定，选独立模式。\n\n2. 准备对话来源：独立模式在「API设置」添加并测试聊天模型；后端或 MCP 先在「Tincall 云端 → 连接云端」部署或连接相应服务，保存连接配置。\n\n3. 配置声音与识别：在「文字转语音」添加并测试声音预设；在「我的设置 → 语音识别」选择识别服务，按所选服务填写凭据并运行测试。\n\n4. 新建或编辑联系人，选择通话方式和声音预设。独立模式再选聊天模型，在「对话设定」填写双方信息、关系背景和对话要求；后端选择连接与对话对象；MCP 选择连接后保存，再把该联系人的完整 MCP 配置复制到对应 AI 平台，并按本页接入指令让 AI 开始等待通话输入。\n\n打开通话页后，按提示补齐缺项，并在首次收音时允许使用麦克风。复制 MCP 配置后，仍需让 AI 在平台中开始等待通话输入。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "1. Choose where replies will come from: select MCP for an AI on a platform that supports MCP; Backend for an existing conversation service adapted for Tincall; or Standalone to configure a model and conversation instructions in Tincall.\n\n2. Prepare that source: for Standalone, add and test a chat model in API Settings. For Backend or MCP, deploy or connect the appropriate service in Tincall Cloud → Connect to Cloud and save the connection.\n\n3. Set up speech: add and test a voice preset in Text to Speech. Select a service in My Settings → Speech Recognition, enter any required credentials, and run its test.\n\n4. Create or edit a contact and select the call mode and voice preset. For Standalone, also select a chat model and fill in Conversation Instructions with information about both participants, their relationship, and conversation preferences. For Backend, select the connection and conversation partner. For MCP, select the connection and save, then copy that contact’s full MCP configuration to the matching AI platform and start the AI using the integration instructions on this page.\n\nOpen the call screen, complete any missing items, and allow microphone access when first using voice input. Copying an MCP configuration does not mean the AI on the platform is already waiting."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "1. 先确定通话方式：要通过支持 MCP 的平台与 AI 通话，选 MCP；已有适配 Tincall 的对话后端，选后端；想在 Tincall 内配置模型和对话设定，选独立模式。\n\n2. 准备对话来源：独立模式在「API设置」添加并测试聊天模型；后端或 MCP 先在「Tincall 云端」部署或连接相应服务，保存连接配置。\n\n3. 配置声音与识别：在「文字转语音」添加并测试声音预设；在「我的设置 → 语音识别」选择识别服务，按所选服务填写凭据并运行测试。\n\n4. 新建或编辑联系人，选择通话方式和声音预设。独立模式再选聊天模型，在「对话设定」填写双方信息、关系背景和对话要求；后端选择连接与对话对象；MCP 选择连接后保存，再在联系人页选择与平台一致的 HTTP 或 SSE，分别复制 URL 和 Authorization 到对应 AI 平台，并按本页接入指令让 AI 开始等待通话输入。\n\n打开通话页后，按提示补齐缺项，并在首次收音时允许使用麦克风。普通 MCP 需让 AI 在平台中开始等待输入；使用唤醒桥时，在已保存服务中复制唤醒配置并接入平台，由事件启动每轮任务。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "1. Choose where replies will come from: select MCP for an AI on a platform that supports MCP; Backend for an existing conversation service adapted for Tincall; or Standalone to configure a model and conversation instructions in Tincall.\n\n2. Prepare that source: for Standalone, add and test a chat model in API Settings. For Backend or MCP, deploy or connect the appropriate service in Tincall Cloud and save the connection.\n\n3. Set up speech: add and test a voice preset in Text to Speech. Select a service in My Settings → Speech Recognition, enter any required credentials, and run its test.\n\n4. Create or edit a contact and select the call mode and voice preset. For Standalone, also select a chat model and fill in Conversation Instructions with information about both participants, their relationship, and conversation preferences. For Backend, select the connection and conversation partner. For MCP, select the connection and save, then copy that contact’s full MCP configuration to the matching AI platform and start the AI using the integration instructions on this page.\n\nOpen the call screen, complete any missing items, and allow microphone access when first using voice input. Copying an MCP configuration does not mean the AI on the platform is already waiting.\n\nFor MCP with the wake bridge, copy the bridge configuration from the saved service and connect it to a compatible platform. Each AI task is started by an event; it does not need to keep a tool waiting. The waiting instructions above apply to ordinary MCP."
          }
        }
