        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tool support, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. Follow the approach you actually use. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Configure the service in the AI platform\nIn Tincall, deploy or connect an MCP-capable service under Settings → Tincall Cloud. Edit a contact, choose MCP and the connection, then save. Copy the complete MCP configuration from the screen shown after saving; later, use View and Copy MCP Configuration in the contact editor. Import it into the matching AI platform’s MCP service settings, use Streamable HTTP, and check the tool list. The configuration contains the full /mcp URL and Authorization: Bearer <contact-specific token>. Do not append /mcp again or substitute the phone access token or a service-role key. Keep tokens in private service settings, not in chat. State clearly if the platform does not support this transport or long-running tool waits.\n\n2. Available tools\nUse tools/list as the authority for parameters and required fields:\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): call the phone. A contact-specific token already selects the identity, so contact_id may be omitted; other credentials must follow the tool schema.\n• tincall_current(): returns {call:object or null}; only reads the current call and does not start or wake an AI.\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?): waits for unanswered input and returns a matching input and job.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?): submits a reply; a complete reply waits for the next turn by default.\n• tincall_inputs(call_id): retrieves saved user inputs and the current reply job; deduplicate by message ID.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): ends the current call.\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?): lists calls for the current identity, newest first. limit defaults to 10 and ranges from 1 to 50.\n• tincall_record(call_id): reads text, saved images, and an optional summary submitted to this connector. No audio is returned. The summary may be empty when disabled, still generating, or failed.\n\n3. Obtain a real call and input\nCall tincall_current first. For an existing call, use its call.id. call:null means there is no current call; do not invent a call_id to wait on. Only when the user asks you to call them, generate new UUIDs for request_id and call_id and invoke tincall_call. Once it returns ringing, use that call.id with tincall_wait_for_input to wait for the phone to answer and for user input. Background delivery also requires push setup on the phone.\n\nFor a call started on the phone, the platform must keep the AI running or have a working wake bridge. After the phone starts the call, use tincall_current to obtain call.id, then wait for input. There is no tool to wait for an incoming call without a call_id. Copying a configuration or calling current does not wake an AI platform.\n\nRetain and follow voice_instructions whenever a wait result includes it, including speech expression requirements. It may be returned only once, even in a result with timed_out:true and input:null. Its absence in later results does not cancel those requirements. Reply only after receiving a non-null input and its matching job; do not invent a user message or an opening-turn job.\n\nTool data is provided in structuredContent or JSON text in content. Images are returned separately as standard MCP image content, preceded by text identifying message_id, image_id, and image_index. Do not rely only on image references in structured data. An image-only input can have empty text; still process its images and matching job.\n\n4. Reply and continue\nGenerate a new request_id for every new submission. Use the current call.id, job.reply_id, and job.epoch. For a complete reply, put the full text in text and set complete:true. When streaming, complete:false sends only the new fragment. The final complete:true must contain the full reply with all previously sent text as its prefix; never rewrite that prefix. The phone handles recognition, synthesis, and playback.\n\ncomplete:true accepts the reply and waits for the next turn by default. If its result already contains input and job, handle that turn directly without waiting again first. wait_for_input:false disables waiting after this submission. A wait defaults to, and cannot exceed, 120 seconds; timeout_seconds ranges from 1 to 120. timed_out:true is not a hangup. Continue with tincall_wait_for_input using the returned after_sequence.\n\nreply_accepted:true with wait_error means the reply was accepted but the subsequent wait failed. Continue using after_sequence without resending accepted text. If a network response is lost, retry with the original request_id and exactly the same parameters. For isError:true, read error.code. stale_epoch means the old job is no longer valid: read the current call and job rather than resending with an old job or epoch.\n\nStop when call.status is ended. Before hanging up, read the latest call state and invoke tincall_end with a new request_id, the existing call.id, and the latest call.epoch. Input, interruption, and hangup can change epoch; do not keep using its initial value. Acceptance of a reply does not mean playback has finished. After the call, use tincall_recent_calls to locate it and tincall_record to read its record and summary.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Tincall Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. A hangup ends the call’s context. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "下面说明如何让 AI 通过 Tincall 通话。MCP 用于支持 MCP 工具的 AI 平台；后端接法用于自行实现通话接口的服务。按实际接法执行，不要把普通模型 API 地址当成 Tincall 后端地址。\n\nMCP 接法\n\n一、在 AI 平台配置服务\n先在 Tincall「设置 → Tincall 云端」部署或连接支持 MCP 的服务，再编辑联系人，通话方式选 MCP、选择连接并保存。在保存后显示的配置页复制完整 MCP 配置；以后可在联系人编辑页点「查看并复制 MCP 配置」。将其导入对应 AI 平台的 MCP 服务设置，传输使用 Streamable HTTP，并检查工具列表。配置包含完整 /mcp 地址及 Authorization: Bearer <联系人专用令牌>，不要重复追加 /mcp，不要用手机访问令牌或 service-role 密钥替代。令牌只放私密服务配置，不贴进聊天。平台不支持该传输或长时间工具等待时，应明确说明。\n\n二、可用工具\n参数及必填项以 tools/list 为准：\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?)：向手机发起来电。联系人专用令牌已选择身份，可省略 contact_id；其他身份按工具要求填写。\n• tincall_current()：返回 {call:对象或null}，只查看当前电话，不启动或唤醒 AI。\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?)：等待未回复输入，返回匹配的 input 和 job。\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?)：提交回复，完整回复默认继续等待下一轮。\n• tincall_inputs(call_id)：补取已保存的用户输入及当前回复任务，按消息 ID 去重。\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch)：结束当前电话。\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?)：按新到旧列出当前身份的通话，limit 默认 10，范围 1–50。\n• tincall_record(call_id)：读取已提交到该连接端的通话文字、图片及可选摘要，不返回音频。摘要关闭、生成中或失败时可能为空。\n\n三、取得真实通话和输入\n先调用 tincall_current。已有电话时使用返回的 call.id；call:null 表示当前没有电话，不能编造 call_id 去等待。用户要求你主动打来时，才生成新的 UUID 作为 request_id 和 call_id 调用 tincall_call；返回 ringing 后即可用该 call.id 调用 tincall_wait_for_input，等待手机接听及用户输入。后台送达还需要手机完成推送配置。\n\n用户从手机拨号时，平台须保持 AI 运行，或已接好真实的唤醒桥；手机开始电话后用 tincall_current 取得 call.id，再等待输入。当前没有不带 call_id 的“等待来电”工具，复制配置或调用 current 也不会自动唤醒 AI 平台。\n\n等待结果中如有 voice_instructions，应立即保留并遵循，包括其中的语音表达要求。它可能只随首次等待返回，即使该次 timed_out:true、input:null 也可能出现；后续字段缺席不代表要求失效。只有拿到非空 input 和匹配的 job 后才回复，不虚构用户发言或首句任务。\n\n工具数据在 structuredContent 或 content 中的 JSON 文本里。图片另以标准 MCP image content 返回，前面的文本给出 message_id、image_id、image_index；不能只读结构化数据中的图片引用。仅图片输入的 text 可以为空，仍需结合图片及匹配任务回复。\n\n四、提交回复并继续通话\n每次新提交生成新的 request_id，使用当前 call.id、job.reply_id 和 job.epoch。完整回复放 text，设 complete:true；如先流式发送，complete:false 的 text 只放本次新增片段，最后 complete:true 必须提交包含已发送前缀的完整正文，不改写前缀。手机负责语音识别、合成及播放。\n\ncomplete:true 默认接受文字后继续等待下一轮。返回中已有 input 和 job 时，直接处理该轮，不再先调用等待。wait_for_input:false 可关闭这次提交后的等待。单次等待默认且最多 120 秒，timeout_seconds 范围 1–120；timed_out:true 不等于挂断，用返回的 after_sequence 调用 tincall_wait_for_input 续等。\n\nreply_accepted:true 且含 wait_error 表示回复已接受、后续等待失败；保留 after_sequence 续等，不重发已接受的文字。网络响应丢失时，重试复用原 request_id 和完全相同的参数。遇到 isError:true 先读取 error.code；stale_epoch 表示旧任务已失效，应重新读取当前电话和任务，不用旧 job 或 epoch 重发。\n\ncall.status 为 ended 时停止。主动挂断前读取最新通话状态，用新的 request_id、已有 call.id 和最新 call.epoch 调用 tincall_end。输入、打断和挂断都可能改变 epoch，不能一直沿用初始值。工具接受回复不表示手机已播完。结束后可用 tincall_recent_calls 找到通话，再用 tincall_record 读取记录与摘要。\n\n后端接法\n\n一、连接与基础格式\n自有后端负责人物设定、上下文和真实生成，手机负责收音、识别、朗读和本地记录。后端实现下面的 HTTPS / JSON 通话接口，无需实现 MCP，也不必开启云端备份。手机在「Tincall 云端 → 连接已有服务」保存 HTTPS 基础地址和手机访问令牌、检查连接，再到联系人编辑页选择后端、该连接及对话对象。\n\n以下路径相对于基础地址。手机发送 Authorization: Bearer <手机访问令牌>，JSON 请求带 Content-Type: application/json 和 Accept: application/json；成功响应为 HTTP 200 的 JSON，不依赖重定向。错误返回非成功 HTTP 状态及 {error:{code:\"错误代码\"}}。写请求按 request_id 去重，相同请求重试返回原结果；同一 ID 不能更改内容。隔离不同访问身份的数据，不让客户端自行声明所有者。\n\ncall 对象必须包含 id(UUID)、contact_id(字符串)、source(\"backend\")、status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\")、epoch(非负整数)、last_sequence(非负整数)。一个 call_id 对应一通电话，message_id 对应一条输入，reply_id 对应一轮回复，不可混用。\n\n二、发现、开始和接听\nGET /capabilities 返回 {bindings:[{contact_id:\"联系人标识\",display_name:\"显示名\",generation_configured:true}]}；display_name 可省略，只有标识非空且 generation_configured:true 的对象才可在手机选择。\n\nPOST /calls 接收 request_id、call_id、contact_id、source:\"backend\"、expression_prompt，返回 {call}；新通话为 active、epoch:0，并产生 call.started 事件。GET /calls/current 返回 {call:对象或null}。如支持后端主动来电，已有 ringing 通话由 POST /calls/{call_id}/answer 接收 request_id、epoch、expression_prompt，返回 active 的 {call}，产生 call.started。expression_prompt 为语音表达要求，可为空；后端负责将其用于生成。\n\n三、输入与回复事件\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input 接收 request_id、message_id、当前 epoch、text，以及可选 images。每张图片为 {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg或image/png\",data_base64:\"标准Base64\"}，最多四张、每张最多 5 MiB，Base64 不带 data URI 前缀。有图时 text 可为空，无图时文字须非空。返回 {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}：input_id 等于 message_id，epoch 已递增一次。保存输入，取消旧生成，并产生 input.accepted、reply.started 后启动本轮生成。\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 返回 {call,events,cursor,has_more}。事件结构为 {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}，sequence 从 1 连续递增。after 默认 0，后续使用上次 cursor；已有事件立即返回，没有则等待新事件或到期返回 events:[]、cursor:N、has_more:false。空页不是挂断；has_more:true 时手机立即续取，不因 call 快照已结束而漏掉尾页。\n\ninput.accepted 和 reply.started 的 payload 包含 input_id、reply_id。reply.delta 另带 delta(新增片段)；reply.completed 另带 text(最终全文，包含已发前缀)；reply.failed 另带 code；reply.interrupted 另带 reason。这些事件的通话、输入、回复和 epoch 必须匹配；手机只接收当前代次，旧结果不得覆盖已保存内容。\n\n四、打断与挂断\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"interrupted\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回保持 active 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.interrupted。POST /calls/{call_id}/end 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"hangup\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回 ended 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.ended。保留已收到文字与中断原因，拒绝旧代次写入；过期代次用 stale_epoch 错误说明。\n\nreply.completed 只结束一句回复。收到 call.ended 或确认 call.status 为 ended 时，结束这通电话的上下文。若要在挂断后将摘要写回其他对话，应由后端的通话结束流程实现并去重，不能把每句完成、空事件页或网络超时当作挂断。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tool support, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. Follow the approach you actually use. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Configure the service in the AI platform\nIn Tincall, deploy or connect an MCP-capable service under Settings → Tincall Cloud. Edit a contact, choose MCP and the connection, then save. Copy the complete MCP configuration from the screen shown after saving; later, use View and Copy MCP Configuration in the contact editor. Import it into the matching AI platform’s MCP service settings, use Streamable HTTP, and check the tool list. The configuration contains the full /mcp URL and Authorization: Bearer <contact-specific token>. Do not append /mcp again or substitute the phone access token or a service-role key. Keep tokens in private service settings, not in chat. State clearly if the platform does not support this transport or long-running tool waits.\n\n2. Available tools\nUse tools/list as the authority for parameters and required fields:\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): call the phone. A contact-specific token already selects the identity, so contact_id may be omitted; other credentials must follow the tool schema.\n• tincall_current(): returns {call:object or null}; only reads the current call and does not start or wake an AI.\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?): waits for unanswered input and returns a matching input and job.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?): submits a reply; a complete reply waits for the next turn by default.\n• tincall_inputs(call_id): retrieves saved user inputs and the current reply job; deduplicate by message ID.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): ends the current call.\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?): lists calls for the current identity, newest first. limit defaults to 10 and ranges from 1 to 50.\n• tincall_record(call_id): reads text, saved images, and an optional summary submitted to this connector. No audio is returned. The summary may be empty when disabled, still generating, or failed.\n\n3. Obtain a real call and input\nCall tincall_current first. For an existing call, use its call.id. call:null means there is no current call; do not invent a call_id to wait on. Only when the user asks you to call them, generate new UUIDs for request_id and call_id and invoke tincall_call. Once it returns ringing, use that call.id with tincall_wait_for_input to wait for the phone to answer and for user input. Background delivery also requires push setup on the phone.\n\nFor a call started on the phone, the platform must keep the AI running or have a working wake bridge. After the phone starts the call, use tincall_current to obtain call.id, then wait for input. There is no tool to wait for an incoming call without a call_id. Copying a configuration or calling current does not wake an AI platform.\n\nRetain and follow voice_instructions whenever a wait result includes it, including speech expression requirements. It may be returned only once, even in a result with timed_out:true and input:null. Its absence in later results does not cancel those requirements. Reply only after receiving a non-null input and its matching job; do not invent a user message or an opening-turn job.\n\nTool data is provided in structuredContent or JSON text in content. Images are returned separately as standard MCP image content, preceded by text identifying message_id, image_id, and image_index. Do not rely only on image references in structured data. An image-only input can have empty text; still process its images and matching job.\n\n4. Reply and continue\nGenerate a new request_id for every new submission. Use the current call.id, job.reply_id, and job.epoch. For a complete reply, put the full text in text and set complete:true. When streaming, complete:false sends only the new fragment. The final complete:true must contain the full reply with all previously sent text as its prefix; never rewrite that prefix. The phone handles recognition, synthesis, and playback.\n\ncomplete:true accepts the reply and waits for the next turn by default. If its result already contains input and job, handle that turn directly without waiting again first. wait_for_input:false disables waiting after this submission. A wait defaults to, and cannot exceed, 120 seconds; timeout_seconds ranges from 1 to 120. timed_out:true is not a hangup. Continue with tincall_wait_for_input using the returned after_sequence.\n\nreply_accepted:true with wait_error means the reply was accepted but the subsequent wait failed. Continue using after_sequence without resending accepted text. If a network response is lost, retry with the original request_id and exactly the same parameters. For isError:true, read error.code. stale_epoch means the old job is no longer valid: read the current call and job rather than resending with an old job or epoch.\n\nStop when call.status is ended. Before hanging up, read the latest call state and invoke tincall_end with a new request_id, the existing call.id, and the latest call.epoch. Input, interruption, and hangup can change epoch; do not keep using its initial value. Acceptance of a reply does not mean playback has finished. After the call, use tincall_recent_calls to locate it and tincall_record to read its record and summary.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Tincall Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. End the call’s context when call.ended is received or call.status is confirmed as ended. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "下面说明如何让 AI 通过 Tincall 通话。MCP 用于支持 MCP 工具的 AI 平台；后端接法用于自行实现通话接口的服务。按实际接法执行，不要把普通模型 API 地址当成 Tincall 后端地址。\n\nMCP 接法\n\n一、在 AI 平台配置服务\n先在 Tincall「设置 → Tincall 云端」部署或连接支持 MCP 的服务，再编辑联系人，通话方式选 MCP、选择连接并保存。联系人页直接提供传输方式、URL 和 Authorization 的复制，推荐 HTTP（Streamable HTTP），平台仅支持旧 SSE 时再选 SSE。将 URL 填入平台 MCP 服务地址，将复制的 Authorization 填入同名请求头；地址已完整，不要重复追加 /mcp。Authorization 包含 Bearer 和联系人专用令牌，不要替换为手机令牌或 service-role 密钥。令牌只放私密服务配置，不贴进聊天。旧云端须升级数据库迁移和服务函数，再刷新平台工具列表。\n\n二、可用工具\n参数及必填项以 tools/list 为准：\n• tincall_call(contact_id?)：向手机发起来电。联系人专用凭据不需要参数；服务自动生成标识，重复拨号复用当前未结束通话。其他身份按工具要求填写 contact_id。\n• tincall_get_call(call_id?, limit?, before_sequence?)：查询通话、当前有效 reply 目标及文字／图片／可选摘要。省略 call_id 查当前通话，没有则 call:null。默认最近 50 条，最多 100；has_more 时用 next_before_sequence 向前翻页。\n• tincall_wait(cursor?)：等待当前通话的 answered、input、interrupted、ended、timeout；返回 call、messages、reply、cursor:{sequence,epoch}。每次默认等待两分钟，不需要选择时长，超时不挂断。\n• tincall_reply(reply_to, text?, status?, wait_for_input?, error_code?, request_id?)：复制最近结果中的 reply.reply_to 并发送本次新增文字，无需生成 UUID。默认 complete，发送后继续等两分钟；wait_for_input:false 立即返回。高级分段发送可用 partial，每段需独立 request_id；failed 不带正文并保留已收到的文字。\n• tincall_end()：立即挂断当前通话，取消当前生成与播放，保留已收到内容。\n• tincall_list_calls(limit?, before?)：按新到旧列出当前身份的通话，默认 10 条、最多 50；将 next_cursor 作为 before 继续查。用 get_call 读具体记录，无录音。\n\n三、接听、回复与续等\n已有通话可用 tincall_get_call 找回。用户要求主动打来时直接调用 tincall_call()，随后调用 tincall_wait()；不需要生成通话或请求 UUID。重复拨号会复用该联系人的未结束通话，创建或推送受理不表示已接听。\n\nanswered 会返回 kind:\"opening\"、input_id:null 的真实开场目标，可以直接问候，不必等用户开口或编造用户发言。用户先提交输入时，旧开场目标失效。input 返回用户的文字／图片与最新 reply 目标；连续补充均按顺序保留。has_more:true 时先用返回的 cursor 续取，直到获得当前有效 reply。复制 reply.reply_to 回复；该标记只用于匹配轮次，鉴权仍由服务配置完成。只读不消费待回复输入，重读按消息 ID 去重。\n\nvoice_instructions 在活动通话的读取和等待结果中可恢复，应遵循其中的语音要求。图片通过 MCP image content 返回，前面的文本标明 message_id、image_id、image_index；不能只读图片引用。仅图片输入的 text 可为空。\n\n通常一次发送完整回复即可；响应丢失时复用相同 reply_to 和文字重试，不重复追加。高级分段发送时，每个 partial 片段生成独立 request_id（UUID），重试沿用该值；text 永远只放本次新增文字，complete 可附最后一段或空 text，不能重发累计全文。status:failed 明确结束失败轮次，error_code 可选，仅小写字母、数字和下划线，最长 64，不能把错误详情写成朗读正文。\n\ncomplete 默认保存文字后继续等待。reply_accepted:true 仅表示服务接受，不表示手机播完；若带 wait_error，只用返回的 cursor 调用 wait，不重发文字。timeout 表示本次等待超时、对方尚未回复，通话继续；按 next_action 调用 tincall_wait 续等，无需为此查询状态；interrupted 时丢弃旧目标继续等；stale_turn 时 get_call 或 wait 恢复，不能向新轮次发送旧回复。ended 时停止。直接调用 tincall_end() 挂断当前通话；end 不保证告别语播完。\n\nMCP＋唤醒桥接法\n\n在已保存服务的「唤醒桥」选择 MCP 联系人并复制接入配置。平台接入程序在模型任务外维持 wake.url 的 SSE 订阅，使用其中的请求头。收到 wake 后，先由接入程序 GET 配置中的 input.url，携带 input.headers；has_more 时将 cursor.sequence 和 cursor.epoch 作为 sequence、epoch 查询参数读完分页，并按消息 ID 去重；取得当前有效回复目标后，再携带文字、实际图片内容、voice_instructions 和 reply.reply_to 启动 AI。AI 连接配置中单独的唤醒桥 MCP，处理已带入的输入，用 tincall_reply 回复；完整回复返回 next_action:finish_task 后结束任务。该 MCP 不提供 tincall_wait，沿用旧指令调用时，会立即提示无需等待并结束本轮。idle／ended 时不启动 AI；输入被新轮次取代时，丢弃旧内容并重新取齐后启动。桥接凭据下读取与完整回复均立即返回。普通 MCP 凭据的默认两分钟等待行为不变。断线按 1–30 秒退避重连，未回复目标会重发；按 event_id 合并重复事件，每位联系人串行处理，始终读取当前轮次，丢弃过期回复。平台须支持事件订阅与任务启动，或运行常驻适配程序；仅导入 MCP 地址不实现唤醒。\n\n四、平台边界\nMCP 工具不能强制取消任意宿主的模型生成，也不能自行唤醒闲置平台；手机拨号需平台保持运行或已有真实唤醒桥。工具超时和连续调用限制取决于平台。平台退出后未结束的 MCP 回复会在五分钟没有写入后由 worker 标为失败，通话仍保留。历史摘要由手机实际提交；null 只说明尚无摘要，不能臆测其原因。\n\n后端接法\n\n一、连接与基础格式\n自有后端负责人物设定、上下文和真实生成，手机负责收音、识别、朗读和本地记录。后端实现下面的 HTTPS / JSON 通话接口，无需实现 MCP，也不必开启云端备份。手机在「Tincall 云端 → 连接已有服务」保存 HTTPS 基础地址和手机访问令牌、检查连接，再到联系人编辑页选择后端、该连接及对话对象。\n\n以下路径相对于基础地址。手机发送 Authorization: Bearer <手机访问令牌>，JSON 请求带 Content-Type: application/json 和 Accept: application/json；成功响应为 HTTP 200 的 JSON，不依赖重定向。错误返回非成功 HTTP 状态及 {error:{code:\"错误代码\"}}。写请求按 request_id 去重，相同请求重试返回原结果；同一 ID 不能更改内容。隔离不同访问身份的数据，不让客户端自行声明所有者。\n\ncall 对象必须包含 id(UUID)、contact_id(字符串)、source(\"backend\")、status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\")、epoch(非负整数)、last_sequence(非负整数)。一个 call_id 对应一通电话，message_id 对应一条输入，reply_id 对应一轮回复，不可混用。\n\n二、发现、开始和接听\nGET /capabilities 返回 {bindings:[{contact_id:\"联系人标识\",display_name:\"显示名\",generation_configured:true}]}；display_name 可省略，只有标识非空且 generation_configured:true 的对象才可在手机选择。\n\nPOST /calls 接收 request_id、call_id、contact_id、source:\"backend\"、expression_prompt，返回 {call}；新通话为 active、epoch:0，并产生 call.started 事件。GET /calls/current 返回 {call:对象或null}。如支持后端主动来电，已有 ringing 通话由 POST /calls/{call_id}/answer 接收 request_id、epoch、expression_prompt，返回 active 的 {call}，产生 call.started。expression_prompt 为语音表达要求，可为空；后端负责将其用于生成。\n\n三、输入与回复事件\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input 接收 request_id、message_id、当前 epoch、text，以及可选 images。每张图片为 {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg或image/png\",data_base64:\"标准Base64\"}，最多四张、每张最多 5 MiB，Base64 不带 data URI 前缀。有图时 text 可为空，无图时文字须非空。返回 {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}：input_id 等于 message_id，epoch 已递增一次。保存输入，取消旧生成，并产生 input.accepted、reply.started 后启动本轮生成。\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 返回 {call,events,cursor,has_more}。事件结构为 {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}，sequence 从 1 连续递增。after 默认 0，后续使用上次 cursor；已有事件立即返回，没有则等待新事件或到期返回 events:[]、cursor:N、has_more:false。空页不是挂断；has_more:true 时手机立即续取，不因 call 快照已结束而漏掉尾页。\n\ninput.accepted 和 reply.started 的 payload 包含 input_id、reply_id。reply.delta 另带 delta(新增片段)；reply.completed 另带 text(最终全文，包含已发前缀)；reply.failed 另带 code；reply.interrupted 另带 reason。这些事件的通话、输入、回复和 epoch 必须匹配；手机只接收当前代次，旧结果不得覆盖已保存内容。\n\n四、打断与挂断\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"interrupted\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回保持 active 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.interrupted。POST /calls/{call_id}/end 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"hangup\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回 ended 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.ended。保留已收到文字与中断原因，拒绝旧代次写入；过期代次用 stale_epoch 错误说明。\n\nreply.completed 只结束一句回复。收到 call.ended 或确认 call.status 为 ended 时，结束这通电话的上下文。若要在挂断后将摘要写回其他对话，应由后端的通话结束流程实现并去重，不能把每句完成、空事件页或网络超时当作挂断。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tools, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Connect\nDeploy or connect a service in Settings → Tincall Cloud. Edit a contact, select MCP and its connection, then save. Copy the URL and Authorization separately from the contact settings. Prefer HTTP (Streamable HTTP); choose legacy SSE only when required. The URL is complete; do not append /mcp again. Authorization already includes Bearer and a contact-specific token. Keep it private; do not substitute a phone token or service-role key. Existing cloud services need the new migration and function, and clients must refresh their tool list.\n\n2. Six tools\nUse tools/list for the exact schema.\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): ring the linked phone. Contact-specific credentials select the identity automatically. Reuse IDs and arguments on retry; creation/push acceptance is not an answer.\n• tincall_get_call(call_id?, limit?, before_sequence?): read state, current reply target, messages/images and optional summary. Omit call_id to recover the current call, or call:null. Latest 50 messages by default, max 100, ascending; next_before_sequence pages backwards while has_more.\n• tincall_wait(call_id, cursor?, timeout_seconds?): wait for answered/input/interrupted/ended/timeout, returning call, messages, reply and cursor:{sequence,epoch}. Default/max 120 seconds; timeout does not hang up.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text?, status?, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?, error_code?): append NEW text. status partial continues, complete finishes (default), failed reports failure with no text and preserves prior fragments. Complete waits by default; wait_for_input:false returns immediately.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): immediately end this call and cancel generation/playback, preserving received content. Does not guarantee goodbye playback.\n• tincall_list_calls(limit?, before?): newest first, default 10/max 50. Pass next_cursor as before to page; get_call reads details. No audio.\n\n3. Call loop\nRecover with get_call first. Only ring when asked, using new request_id/call_id UUIDs, then wait. answered returns a real opening target (kind:opening, input_id:null); greet without inventing user speech. User input invalidates the old opener. input contains all new messages and the latest reply target. With has_more:true, keep draining with cursor before replying. Reads do not acknowledge unanswered input; deduplicate repeated message IDs.\n\nFollow recoverable voice_instructions. Images arrive as MCP image content preceded by message_id/image_id/image_index text; references alone are not image content. Image-only messages may have empty text.\n\n4. Replies and recovery\nUse reply.reply_id and reply.epoch. Every new fragment gets a new request_id; every retry reuses the same ID and mutation fields. text always contains only NEW text, even on complete. Complete may send a final fragment or empty text; never resend the accumulated reply. Appends and finalization are atomic. failed optionally accepts an error_code with lowercase letters/digits/underscores, max 64; never put diagnostic details into spoken text.\n\nComplete waits for the next event. reply_accepted:true means stored, not played. With wait_error, only resume wait using cursor; do not resend accepted text. On timeout, continue wait with cursor. On interrupted, discard the old target and wait. On stale_turn, recover through get_call/wait and discard stale output. On ended, stop. End uses the latest call.epoch.\n\n5. Platform limits\nMCP cannot force-cancel arbitrary host generation or wake an idle AI. Phone-originated calls require a running host or a real wake bridge. Host tool timeouts and consecutive-tool limits still apply. Abandoned MCP targets fail via the worker after five minutes without a write; the call stays active. Summaries contain only what the phone submitted; null does not identify a summary lifecycle state.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Tincall Cloud → Connect to Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. End the call’s context when call.ended is received or call.status is confirmed as ended. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup.\n\nOptional MCP wake bridge: Copy a contact configuration from Wake Bridge in the saved service. Outside model tasks, the platform adapter keeps an SSE subscription to wake.url with its headers. On each wake, the adapter FIRST sends GET to input.url with input.headers. Drain has_more pages by passing cursor.sequence and cursor.epoch as sequence and epoch query parameters, deduplicating messages by ID. It THEN starts the AI with all messages, actual image content, voice_instructions and the latest reply.reply_to. The AI connects to the dedicated wake MCP and replies through tincall_reply. A complete reply returns next_action:finish_task. End that task. This MCP does not expose tincall_wait; obsolete wait calls return a friendly normal response indicating that no waiting is needed and this task can finish. On idle/ended, do not start the AI. Discard superseded work and recover the current input before starting a fresh task. Bridge reads and complete replies return immediately. Ordinary MCP credentials keep the default two-minute wait. Reconnect with 1–30 second backoff. Pending targets replay; coalesce duplicate event_id values and serialize tasks per contact. Always recover the current target after interruptions and discard stale generated replies. The platform must support subscribing and starting tasks or run a persistent adapter. MCP settings alone do not provide wake support."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "下面说明如何让 AI 通过 Tincall 通话。MCP 用于支持 MCP 工具的 AI 平台；后端接法用于自行实现通话接口的服务。按实际接法执行，不要把普通模型 API 地址当成 Tincall 后端地址。\n\nMCP 接法\n\n一、在 AI 平台配置服务\n先在 Tincall「设置 → Tincall 云端」部署或连接支持 MCP 的服务，再编辑联系人，通话方式选 MCP、选择连接并保存。联系人页直接提供传输方式、URL 和 Authorization 的复制，推荐 HTTP（Streamable HTTP），平台仅支持旧 SSE 时再选 SSE。将 URL 填入平台 MCP 服务地址，将复制的 Authorization 填入同名请求头；地址已完整，不要重复追加 /mcp。Authorization 包含 Bearer 和联系人专用令牌，不要替换为手机令牌或 service-role 密钥。令牌只放私密服务配置，不贴进聊天。旧云端须升级数据库迁移和服务函数，再刷新平台工具列表。\n\n二、可用工具\n参数及必填项以 tools/list 为准：\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?)：向手机发起来电。联系人专用令牌已选择身份，可省略 contact_id；其他身份按工具要求填写。\n• tincall_get_call(call_id?, limit?, before_sequence?)：查询通话、当前有效 reply 目标及文字／图片／可选摘要。省略 call_id 查当前通话，没有则 call:null。默认最近 50 条，最多 100；has_more 时用 next_before_sequence 向前翻页。\n• tincall_wait(call_id, cursor?, timeout_seconds?)：等待 answered、input、interrupted、ended、timeout；返回 call、messages、reply、cursor:{sequence,epoch}。默认／最多 120 秒，超时不挂断。\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text?, status?, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?, error_code?)：追加本次新增文字，status 为 partial／complete／failed，默认 complete。complete 默认接着等待下一轮，wait_for_input:false 立即返回；failed 不带正文，保留已收到的文字。\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch)：立即挂断，取消当前生成与播放，保留已收到内容。\n• tincall_list_calls(limit?, before?)：按新到旧列出当前身份的通话，默认 10 条、最多 50；将 next_cursor 作为 before 继续查。用 get_call 读具体记录，无录音。\n\n三、接听、回复与续等\n先用 tincall_get_call 找回当前通话。用户要求主动打来时，生成 request_id、call_id 两个 UUID 并调用 tincall_call；失败重试沿用原值和原参数，不能另外拨一通。创建或推送受理不表示已接听；随后调用 tincall_wait。\n\nanswered 会返回 kind:\"opening\"、input_id:null 的真实开场目标，可以直接问候，不必等用户开口或编造用户发言。用户先提交输入时，旧开场目标失效。input 返回用户的文字／图片与最新 reply 目标；连续补充均按顺序保留。has_more:true 时先用返回的 cursor 续取，直到获得当前有效 reply。按 reply.reply_id、reply.epoch 回复。只读不消费待回复输入，重读按消息 ID 去重。\n\nvoice_instructions 在活动通话的读取和等待结果中可恢复，应遵循其中的语音要求。图片通过 MCP image content 返回，前面的文本标明 message_id、image_id、image_index；不能只读图片引用。仅图片输入的 text 可为空。\n\n每个新片段生成新 request_id；text 永远只放本次新增文字。partial 继续，complete 可附最后一段或空 text，仅结束该回复，不能重发全文。追加与完成原子保存，响应丢失重试复用原 request_id 和相同参数，不重复朗读。status:failed 明确结束失败轮次，error_code 可选，仅小写字母、数字和下划线，最长 64，不能把错误详情写成朗读正文。\n\ncomplete 默认保存文字后继续等待。reply_accepted:true 仅表示服务接受，不表示手机播完；若带 wait_error，只用返回的 cursor 调用 wait，不重发文字。timeout 时用返回 cursor 续等；interrupted 时丢弃旧目标继续等；stale_turn 时 get_call 或 wait 恢复，不能向新轮次发送旧回复。ended 时停止。挂断用最新 call.epoch，不能一直沿用初值；end 不保证告别语播完。\n\n四、平台边界\nMCP 工具不能强制取消任意宿主的模型生成，也不能自行唤醒闲置平台；手机拨号需平台保持运行或已有真实唤醒桥。工具超时和连续调用限制取决于平台。平台退出后未结束的 MCP 回复会在五分钟没有写入后由 worker 标为失败，通话仍保留。历史摘要由手机实际提交；null 只说明尚无摘要，不能臆测其原因。\n\n后端接法\n\n一、连接与基础格式\n自有后端负责人物设定、上下文和真实生成，手机负责收音、识别、朗读和本地记录。后端实现下面的 HTTPS / JSON 通话接口，无需实现 MCP，也不必开启云端备份。手机在「Tincall 云端 → 连接已有服务」保存 HTTPS 基础地址和手机访问令牌、检查连接，再到联系人编辑页选择后端、该连接及对话对象。\n\n以下路径相对于基础地址。手机发送 Authorization: Bearer <手机访问令牌>，JSON 请求带 Content-Type: application/json 和 Accept: application/json；成功响应为 HTTP 200 的 JSON，不依赖重定向。错误返回非成功 HTTP 状态及 {error:{code:\"错误代码\"}}。写请求按 request_id 去重，相同请求重试返回原结果；同一 ID 不能更改内容。隔离不同访问身份的数据，不让客户端自行声明所有者。\n\ncall 对象必须包含 id(UUID)、contact_id(字符串)、source(\"backend\")、status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\")、epoch(非负整数)、last_sequence(非负整数)。一个 call_id 对应一通电话，message_id 对应一条输入，reply_id 对应一轮回复，不可混用。\n\n二、发现、开始和接听\nGET /capabilities 返回 {bindings:[{contact_id:\"联系人标识\",display_name:\"显示名\",generation_configured:true}]}；display_name 可省略，只有标识非空且 generation_configured:true 的对象才可在手机选择。\n\nPOST /calls 接收 request_id、call_id、contact_id、source:\"backend\"、expression_prompt，返回 {call}；新通话为 active、epoch:0，并产生 call.started 事件。GET /calls/current 返回 {call:对象或null}。如支持后端主动来电，已有 ringing 通话由 POST /calls/{call_id}/answer 接收 request_id、epoch、expression_prompt，返回 active 的 {call}，产生 call.started。expression_prompt 为语音表达要求，可为空；后端负责将其用于生成。\n\n三、输入与回复事件\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input 接收 request_id、message_id、当前 epoch、text，以及可选 images。每张图片为 {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg或image/png\",data_base64:\"标准Base64\"}，最多四张、每张最多 5 MiB，Base64 不带 data URI 前缀。有图时 text 可为空，无图时文字须非空。返回 {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}：input_id 等于 message_id，epoch 已递增一次。保存输入，取消旧生成，并产生 input.accepted、reply.started 后启动本轮生成。\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 返回 {call,events,cursor,has_more}。事件结构为 {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}，sequence 从 1 连续递增。after 默认 0，后续使用上次 cursor；已有事件立即返回，没有则等待新事件或到期返回 events:[]、cursor:N、has_more:false。空页不是挂断；has_more:true 时手机立即续取，不因 call 快照已结束而漏掉尾页。\n\ninput.accepted 和 reply.started 的 payload 包含 input_id、reply_id。reply.delta 另带 delta(新增片段)；reply.completed 另带 text(最终全文，包含已发前缀)；reply.failed 另带 code；reply.interrupted 另带 reason。这些事件的通话、输入、回复和 epoch 必须匹配；手机只接收当前代次，旧结果不得覆盖已保存内容。\n\n四、打断与挂断\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"interrupted\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回保持 active 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.interrupted。POST /calls/{call_id}/end 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"hangup\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回 ended 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.ended。保留已收到文字与中断原因，拒绝旧代次写入；过期代次用 stale_epoch 错误说明。\n\nreply.completed 只结束一句回复。收到 call.ended 或确认 call.status 为 ended 时，结束这通电话的上下文。若要在挂断后将摘要写回其他对话，应由后端的通话结束流程实现并去重，不能把每句完成、空事件页或网络超时当作挂断。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tools, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Connect\nDeploy or connect a service in Settings → Tincall Cloud. Edit a contact, select MCP and its connection, then save. Copy the URL and Authorization separately from the contact settings. Prefer HTTP (Streamable HTTP); choose legacy SSE only when required. The URL is complete; do not append /mcp again. Authorization already includes Bearer and a contact-specific token. Keep it private; do not substitute a phone token or service-role key. Existing cloud services need the new migration and function, and clients must refresh their tool list.\n\n2. Six tools\nUse tools/list for the exact schema.\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): ring the linked phone. Contact-specific credentials select the identity automatically. Reuse IDs and arguments on retry; creation/push acceptance is not an answer.\n• tincall_get_call(call_id?, limit?, before_sequence?): read state, current reply target, messages/images and optional summary. Omit call_id to recover the current call, or call:null. Latest 50 messages by default, max 100, ascending; next_before_sequence pages backwards while has_more.\n• tincall_wait(call_id, cursor?, timeout_seconds?): wait for answered/input/interrupted/ended/timeout, returning call, messages, reply and cursor:{sequence,epoch}. Default/max 120 seconds; timeout does not hang up.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text?, status?, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?, error_code?): append NEW text. status partial continues, complete finishes (default), failed reports failure with no text and preserves prior fragments. Complete waits by default; wait_for_input:false returns immediately.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): immediately end this call and cancel generation/playback, preserving received content. Does not guarantee goodbye playback.\n• tincall_list_calls(limit?, before?): newest first, default 10/max 50. Pass next_cursor as before to page; get_call reads details. No audio.\n\n3. Call loop\nRecover with get_call first. Only ring when asked, using new request_id/call_id UUIDs, then wait. answered returns a real opening target (kind:opening, input_id:null); greet without inventing user speech. User input invalidates the old opener. input contains all new messages and the latest reply target. With has_more:true, keep draining with cursor before replying. Reads do not acknowledge unanswered input; deduplicate repeated message IDs.\n\nFollow recoverable voice_instructions. Images arrive as MCP image content preceded by message_id/image_id/image_index text; references alone are not image content. Image-only messages may have empty text.\n\n4. Replies and recovery\nUse reply.reply_id and reply.epoch. Every new fragment gets a new request_id; every retry reuses the same ID and mutation fields. text always contains only NEW text, even on complete. Complete may send a final fragment or empty text; never resend the accumulated reply. Appends and finalization are atomic. failed optionally accepts an error_code with lowercase letters/digits/underscores, max 64; never put diagnostic details into spoken text.\n\nComplete waits for the next event. reply_accepted:true means stored, not played. With wait_error, only resume wait using cursor; do not resend accepted text. On timeout, continue wait with cursor. On interrupted, discard the old target and wait. On stale_turn, recover through get_call/wait and discard stale output. On ended, stop. End uses the latest call.epoch.\n\n5. Platform limits\nMCP cannot force-cancel arbitrary host generation or wake an idle AI. Phone-originated calls require a running host or a real wake bridge. Host tool timeouts and consecutive-tool limits still apply. Abandoned MCP targets fail via the worker after five minutes without a write; the call stays active. Summaries contain only what the phone submitted; null does not identify a summary lifecycle state.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Tincall Cloud → Connect to Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. End the call’s context when call.ended is received or call.status is confirmed as ended. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "下面说明如何让 AI 通过 Tincall 通话。MCP 用于支持 MCP 工具的 AI 平台；后端接法用于自行实现通话接口的服务。按实际接法执行，不要把普通模型 API 地址当成 Tincall 后端地址。\n\nMCP 接法\n\n一、在 AI 平台配置服务\n先在 Tincall「设置 → 云端同步与来电 → 连接云端」部署或连接支持 MCP 的服务，再编辑联系人，通话方式选 MCP、选择连接并保存。在保存后显示的配置页复制完整 MCP 配置；以后可在联系人编辑页点「查看并复制 MCP 配置」。将其导入对应 AI 平台的 MCP 服务设置，传输使用 Streamable HTTP，并检查工具列表。配置包含完整 /mcp 地址及 Authorization: Bearer <联系人专用令牌>，不要重复追加 /mcp，不要用手机访问令牌或 service-role 密钥替代。令牌只放私密服务配置，不贴进聊天。平台不支持该传输或长时间工具等待时，应明确说明。\n\n二、可用工具\n参数及必填项以 tools/list 为准：\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?)：向手机发起来电。联系人专用令牌已选择身份，可省略 contact_id；其他身份按工具要求填写。\n• tincall_current()：返回 {call:对象或null}，只查看当前电话，不启动或唤醒 AI。\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?)：等待未回复输入，返回匹配的 input 和 job。\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?)：提交回复，完整回复默认继续等待下一轮。\n• tincall_inputs(call_id)：补取已保存的用户输入及当前回复任务，按消息 ID 去重。\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch)：结束当前电话。\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?)：按新到旧列出当前身份的通话，limit 默认 10，范围 1–50。\n• tincall_record(call_id)：读取已提交到该连接端的通话文字、图片及可选摘要，不返回音频。摘要关闭、生成中或失败时可能为空。\n\n三、取得真实通话和输入\n先调用 tincall_current。已有电话时使用返回的 call.id；call:null 表示当前没有电话，不能编造 call_id 去等待。用户要求你主动打来时，才生成新的 UUID 作为 request_id 和 call_id 调用 tincall_call；返回 ringing 后即可用该 call.id 调用 tincall_wait_for_input，等待手机接听及用户输入。后台送达还需要手机完成推送配置。\n\n用户从手机拨号时，平台须保持 AI 运行，或已接好真实的唤醒桥；手机开始电话后用 tincall_current 取得 call.id，再等待输入。当前没有不带 call_id 的“等待来电”工具，复制配置或调用 current 也不会自动唤醒 AI 平台。\n\n等待结果中如有 voice_instructions，应立即保留并遵循，包括其中的语音表达要求。它可能只随首次等待返回，即使该次 timed_out:true、input:null 也可能出现；后续字段缺席不代表要求失效。只有拿到非空 input 和匹配的 job 后才回复，不虚构用户发言或首句任务。\n\n工具数据在 structuredContent 或 content 中的 JSON 文本里。图片另以标准 MCP image content 返回，前面的文本给出 message_id、image_id、image_index；不能只读结构化数据中的图片引用。仅图片输入的 text 可以为空，仍需结合图片及匹配任务回复。\n\n四、提交回复并继续通话\n每次新提交生成新的 request_id，使用当前 call.id、job.reply_id 和 job.epoch。完整回复放 text，设 complete:true；如先流式发送，complete:false 的 text 只放本次新增片段，最后 complete:true 必须提交包含已发送前缀的完整正文，不改写前缀。手机负责语音识别、合成及播放。\n\ncomplete:true 默认接受文字后继续等待下一轮。返回中已有 input 和 job 时，直接处理该轮，不再先调用等待。wait_for_input:false 可关闭这次提交后的等待。单次等待默认且最多 120 秒，timeout_seconds 范围 1–120；timed_out:true 不等于挂断，用返回的 after_sequence 调用 tincall_wait_for_input 续等。\n\nreply_accepted:true 且含 wait_error 表示回复已接受、后续等待失败；保留 after_sequence 续等，不重发已接受的文字。网络响应丢失时，重试复用原 request_id 和完全相同的参数。遇到 isError:true 先读取 error.code；stale_epoch 表示旧任务已失效，应重新读取当前电话和任务，不用旧 job 或 epoch 重发。\n\ncall.status 为 ended 时停止。主动挂断前读取最新通话状态，用新的 request_id、已有 call.id 和最新 call.epoch 调用 tincall_end。输入、打断和挂断都可能改变 epoch，不能一直沿用初始值。工具接受回复不表示手机已播完。结束后可用 tincall_recent_calls 找到通话，再用 tincall_record 读取记录与摘要。\n\n后端接法\n\n一、连接与基础格式\n自有后端负责人物设定、上下文和真实生成，手机负责收音、识别、朗读和本地记录。后端实现下面的 HTTPS / JSON 通话接口，无需实现 MCP，也不必开启云端备份。手机在「云端同步与来电 → 连接云端 → 连接已有服务」保存 HTTPS 基础地址和手机访问令牌、检查连接，再到联系人编辑页选择后端、该连接及对话对象。\n\n以下路径相对于基础地址。手机发送 Authorization: Bearer <手机访问令牌>，JSON 请求带 Content-Type: application/json 和 Accept: application/json；成功响应为 HTTP 200 的 JSON，不依赖重定向。错误返回非成功 HTTP 状态及 {error:{code:\"错误代码\"}}。写请求按 request_id 去重，相同请求重试返回原结果；同一 ID 不能更改内容。隔离不同访问身份的数据，不让客户端自行声明所有者。\n\ncall 对象必须包含 id(UUID)、contact_id(字符串)、source(\"backend\")、status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\")、epoch(非负整数)、last_sequence(非负整数)。一个 call_id 对应一通电话，message_id 对应一条输入，reply_id 对应一轮回复，不可混用。\n\n二、发现、开始和接听\nGET /capabilities 返回 {bindings:[{contact_id:\"联系人标识\",display_name:\"显示名\",generation_configured:true}]}；display_name 可省略，只有标识非空且 generation_configured:true 的对象才可在手机选择。\n\nPOST /calls 接收 request_id、call_id、contact_id、source:\"backend\"、expression_prompt，返回 {call}；新通话为 active、epoch:0，并产生 call.started 事件。GET /calls/current 返回 {call:对象或null}。如支持后端主动来电，已有 ringing 通话由 POST /calls/{call_id}/answer 接收 request_id、epoch、expression_prompt，返回 active 的 {call}，产生 call.started。expression_prompt 为语音表达要求，可为空；后端负责将其用于生成。\n\n三、输入与回复事件\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input 接收 request_id、message_id、当前 epoch、text，以及可选 images。每张图片为 {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg或image/png\",data_base64:\"标准Base64\"}，最多四张、每张最多 5 MiB，Base64 不带 data URI 前缀。有图时 text 可为空，无图时文字须非空。返回 {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}：input_id 等于 message_id，epoch 已递增一次。保存输入，取消旧生成，并产生 input.accepted、reply.started 后启动本轮生成。\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 返回 {call,events,cursor,has_more}。事件结构为 {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}，sequence 从 1 连续递增。after 默认 0，后续使用上次 cursor；已有事件立即返回，没有则等待新事件或到期返回 events:[]、cursor:N、has_more:false。空页不是挂断；has_more:true 时手机立即续取，不因 call 快照已结束而漏掉尾页。\n\ninput.accepted 和 reply.started 的 payload 包含 input_id、reply_id。reply.delta 另带 delta(新增片段)；reply.completed 另带 text(最终全文，包含已发前缀)；reply.failed 另带 code；reply.interrupted 另带 reason。这些事件的通话、输入、回复和 epoch 必须匹配；手机只接收当前代次，旧结果不得覆盖已保存内容。\n\n四、打断与挂断\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"interrupted\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回保持 active 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.interrupted。POST /calls/{call_id}/end 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"hangup\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回 ended 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.ended。保留已收到文字与中断原因，拒绝旧代次写入；过期代次用 stale_epoch 错误说明。\n\nreply.completed 只结束一句回复，只有挂断才结束这通电话的上下文。若要在挂断后将摘要写回其他对话，应由后端的通话结束流程实现并去重，不能把每句完成、空事件页或网络超时当作挂断。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tool support, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. Follow the approach you actually use. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Configure the service in the AI platform\nIn Tincall, deploy or connect an MCP-capable service under Settings → Cloud Sync & Calls → Connect to Cloud. Edit a contact, choose MCP and the connection, then save. Copy the complete MCP configuration from the screen shown after saving; later, use View and Copy MCP Configuration in the contact editor. Import it into the matching AI platform’s MCP service settings, use Streamable HTTP, and check the tool list. The configuration contains the full /mcp URL and Authorization: Bearer <contact-specific token>. Do not append /mcp again or substitute the phone access token or a service-role key. Keep tokens in private service settings, not in chat. State clearly if the platform does not support this transport or long-running tool waits.\n\n2. Available tools\nUse tools/list as the authority for parameters and required fields:\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): call the phone. A contact-specific token already selects the identity, so contact_id may be omitted; other credentials must follow the tool schema.\n• tincall_current(): returns {call:object or null}; only reads the current call and does not start or wake an AI.\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?): waits for unanswered input and returns a matching input and job.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?): submits a reply; a complete reply waits for the next turn by default.\n• tincall_inputs(call_id): retrieves saved user inputs and the current reply job; deduplicate by message ID.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): ends the current call.\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?): lists calls for the current identity, newest first. limit defaults to 10 and ranges from 1 to 50.\n• tincall_record(call_id): reads text, saved images, and an optional summary submitted to this connector. No audio is returned. The summary may be empty when disabled, still generating, or failed.\n\n3. Obtain a real call and input\nCall tincall_current first. For an existing call, use its call.id. call:null means there is no current call; do not invent a call_id to wait on. Only when the user asks you to call them, generate new UUIDs for request_id and call_id and invoke tincall_call. Once it returns ringing, use that call.id with tincall_wait_for_input to wait for the phone to answer and for user input. Background delivery also requires push setup on the phone.\n\nFor a call started on the phone, the platform must keep the AI running or have a working wake bridge. After the phone starts the call, use tincall_current to obtain call.id, then wait for input. There is no tool to wait for an incoming call without a call_id. Copying a configuration or calling current does not wake an AI platform.\n\nRetain and follow voice_instructions whenever a wait result includes it, including speech expression requirements. It may be returned only once, even in a result with timed_out:true and input:null. Its absence in later results does not cancel those requirements. Reply only after receiving a non-null input and its matching job; do not invent a user message or an opening-turn job.\n\nTool data is provided in structuredContent or JSON text in content. Images are returned separately as standard MCP image content, preceded by text identifying message_id, image_id, and image_index. Do not rely only on image references in structured data. An image-only input can have empty text; still process its images and matching job.\n\n4. Reply and continue\nGenerate a new request_id for every new submission. Use the current call.id, job.reply_id, and job.epoch. For a complete reply, put the full text in text and set complete:true. When streaming, complete:false sends only the new fragment. The final complete:true must contain the full reply with all previously sent text as its prefix; never rewrite that prefix. The phone handles recognition, synthesis, and playback.\n\ncomplete:true accepts the reply and waits for the next turn by default. If its result already contains input and job, handle that turn directly without waiting again first. wait_for_input:false disables waiting after this submission. A wait defaults to, and cannot exceed, 120 seconds; timeout_seconds ranges from 1 to 120. timed_out:true is not a hangup. Continue with tincall_wait_for_input using the returned after_sequence.\n\nreply_accepted:true with wait_error means the reply was accepted but the subsequent wait failed. Continue using after_sequence without resending accepted text. If a network response is lost, retry with the original request_id and exactly the same parameters. For isError:true, read error.code. stale_epoch means the old job is no longer valid: read the current call and job rather than resending with an old job or epoch.\n\nStop when call.status is ended. Before hanging up, read the latest call state and invoke tincall_end with a new request_id, the existing call.id, and the latest call.epoch. Input, interruption, and hangup can change epoch; do not keep using its initial value. Acceptance of a reply does not mean playback has finished. After the call, use tincall_recent_calls to locate it and tincall_record to read its record and summary.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Cloud Sync & Calls → Connect to Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. A hangup ends the call’s context. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "下面说明如何让 AI 通过 Tincall 通话。MCP 用于支持 MCP 工具的 AI 平台；后端接法用于自行实现通话接口的服务。按实际接法执行，不要把普通模型 API 地址当成 Tincall 后端地址。\n\nMCP 接法\n\n一、在 AI 平台配置服务\n先在 Tincall「设置 → 云端同步与来电 → 连接云端」部署或连接支持 MCP 的服务，再编辑联系人，通话方式选 MCP、选择连接并保存。在保存后显示的配置页复制完整 MCP 配置；以后可在联系人编辑页点「查看并复制 MCP 配置」。将其导入对应 AI 平台的 MCP 服务设置，传输使用 Streamable HTTP，并检查工具列表。配置包含完整 /mcp 地址及 Authorization: Bearer <联系人专用令牌>，不要重复追加 /mcp，不要用手机访问令牌或 service-role 密钥替代。令牌只放私密服务配置，不贴进聊天。平台不支持该传输或长时间工具等待时，应明确说明。\n\n二、可用工具\n参数及必填项以 tools/list 为准：\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?)：向手机发起来电。联系人专用令牌已选择身份，可省略 contact_id；其他身份按工具要求填写。\n• tincall_current()：返回 {call:对象或null}，只查看当前电话，不启动或唤醒 AI。\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?)：等待未回复输入，返回匹配的 input 和 job。\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?)：提交回复，完整回复默认继续等待下一轮。\n• tincall_inputs(call_id)：补取已保存的用户输入及当前回复任务，按消息 ID 去重。\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch)：结束当前电话。\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?)：按新到旧列出当前身份的通话，limit 默认 10，范围 1–50。\n• tincall_record(call_id)：读取已提交到该连接端的通话文字、图片及可选摘要，不返回音频。摘要关闭、生成中或失败时可能为空。\n\n三、取得真实通话和输入\n先调用 tincall_current。已有电话时使用返回的 call.id；call:null 表示当前没有电话，不能编造 call_id 去等待。用户要求你主动打来时，才生成新的 UUID 作为 request_id 和 call_id 调用 tincall_call；返回 ringing 后即可用该 call.id 调用 tincall_wait_for_input，等待手机接听及用户输入。后台送达还需要手机完成推送配置。\n\n用户从手机拨号时，平台须保持 AI 运行，或已接好真实的唤醒桥；手机开始电话后用 tincall_current 取得 call.id，再等待输入。当前没有不带 call_id 的“等待来电”工具，复制配置或调用 current 也不会自动唤醒 AI 平台。\n\n等待结果中如有 voice_instructions，应立即保留并遵循，包括其中的语音表达要求。它可能只随首次等待返回，即使该次 timed_out:true、input:null 也可能出现；后续字段缺席不代表要求失效。只有拿到非空 input 和匹配的 job 后才回复，不虚构用户发言或首句任务。\n\n工具数据在 structuredContent 或 content 中的 JSON 文本里。图片另以标准 MCP image content 返回，前面的文本给出 message_id、image_id、image_index；不能只读结构化数据中的图片引用。仅图片输入的 text 可以为空，仍需结合图片及匹配任务回复。\n\n四、提交回复并继续通话\n每次新提交生成新的 request_id，使用当前 call.id、job.reply_id 和 job.epoch。完整回复放 text，设 complete:true；如先流式发送，complete:false 的 text 只放本次新增片段，最后 complete:true 必须提交包含已发送前缀的完整正文，不改写前缀。手机负责语音识别、合成及播放。\n\ncomplete:true 默认接受文字后继续等待下一轮。返回中已有 input 和 job 时，直接处理该轮，不再先调用等待。wait_for_input:false 可关闭这次提交后的等待。单次等待默认且最多 120 秒，timeout_seconds 范围 1–120；timed_out:true 不等于挂断，用返回的 after_sequence 调用 tincall_wait_for_input 续等。\n\nreply_accepted:true 且含 wait_error 表示回复已接受、后续等待失败；保留 after_sequence 续等，不重发已接受的文字。网络响应丢失时，重试复用原 request_id 和完全相同的参数。遇到 isError:true 先读取 error.code；stale_epoch 表示旧任务已失效，应重新读取当前电话和任务，不用旧 job 或 epoch 重发。\n\ncall.status 为 ended 时停止。主动挂断前读取最新通话状态，用新的 request_id、已有 call.id 和最新 call.epoch 调用 tincall_end。输入、打断和挂断都可能改变 epoch，不能一直沿用初始值。工具接受回复不表示手机已播完。结束后可用 tincall_recent_calls 找到通话，再用 tincall_record 读取记录与摘要。\n\n后端接法\n\n一、连接与基础格式\n自有后端负责人物设定、上下文和真实生成，手机负责收音、识别、朗读和本地记录。后端实现下面的 HTTPS / JSON 通话接口，无需实现 MCP，也不必开启云端备份。手机在「云端同步与来电 → 连接云端 → 连接已有服务」保存 HTTPS 基础地址和手机访问令牌、检查连接，再到联系人编辑页选择后端、该连接及对话对象。\n\n以下路径相对于基础地址。手机发送 Authorization: Bearer <手机访问令牌>，JSON 请求带 Content-Type: application/json 和 Accept: application/json；成功响应为 HTTP 200 的 JSON，不依赖重定向。错误返回非成功 HTTP 状态及 {error:{code:\"错误代码\"}}。写请求按 request_id 去重，相同请求重试返回原结果；同一 ID 不能更改内容。隔离不同访问身份的数据，不让客户端自行声明所有者。\n\ncall 对象必须包含 id(UUID)、contact_id(字符串)、source(\"backend\")、status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\")、epoch(非负整数)、last_sequence(非负整数)。一个 call_id 对应一通电话，message_id 对应一条输入，reply_id 对应一轮回复，不可混用。\n\n二、发现、开始和接听\nGET /capabilities 返回 {bindings:[{contact_id:\"联系人标识\",display_name:\"显示名\",generation_configured:true}]}；display_name 可省略，只有标识非空且 generation_configured:true 的对象才可在手机选择。\n\nPOST /calls 接收 request_id、call_id、contact_id、source:\"backend\"、expression_prompt，返回 {call}；新通话为 active、epoch:0，并产生 call.started 事件。GET /calls/current 返回 {call:对象或null}。如支持后端主动来电，已有 ringing 通话由 POST /calls/{call_id}/answer 接收 request_id、epoch、expression_prompt，返回 active 的 {call}，产生 call.started。expression_prompt 为语音表达要求，可为空；后端负责将其用于生成。\n\n三、输入与回复事件\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input 接收 request_id、message_id、当前 epoch、text，以及可选 images。每张图片为 {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg或image/png\",data_base64:\"标准Base64\"}，最多四张、每张最多 5 MiB，Base64 不带 data URI 前缀。有图时 text 可为空，无图时文字须非空。返回 {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}：input_id 等于 message_id，epoch 已递增一次。保存输入，取消旧生成，并产生 input.accepted、reply.started 后启动本轮生成。\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 返回 {call,events,cursor,has_more}。事件结构为 {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}，sequence 从 1 连续递增。after 默认 0，后续使用上次 cursor；已有事件立即返回，没有则等待新事件或到期返回 events:[]、cursor:N、has_more:false。空页不是挂断；has_more:true 时手机立即续取，不因 call 快照已结束而漏掉尾页。\n\ninput.accepted 和 reply.started 的 payload 包含 input_id、reply_id。reply.delta 另带 delta(新增片段)；reply.completed 另带 text(最终全文，包含已发前缀)；reply.failed 另带 code；reply.interrupted 另带 reason。这些事件的通话、输入、回复和 epoch 必须匹配；手机只接收当前代次，旧结果不得覆盖已保存内容。\n\n四、打断与挂断\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"interrupted\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回保持 active 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.interrupted。POST /calls/{call_id}/end 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"hangup\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回 ended 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.ended。保留已收到文字与中断原因，拒绝旧代次写入；过期代次用 stale_epoch 错误说明。\n\nreply.completed 只结束一句回复。收到 call.ended 或确认 call.status 为 ended 时，结束这通电话的上下文。若要在挂断后将摘要写回其他对话，应由后端的通话结束流程实现并去重，不能把每句完成、空事件页或网络超时当作挂断。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tool support, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. Follow the approach you actually use. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Configure the service in the AI platform\nIn Tincall, deploy or connect an MCP-capable service under Settings → Cloud Sync & Calls → Connect to Cloud. Edit a contact, choose MCP and the connection, then save. Copy the complete MCP configuration from the screen shown after saving; later, use View and Copy MCP Configuration in the contact editor. Import it into the matching AI platform’s MCP service settings, use Streamable HTTP, and check the tool list. The configuration contains the full /mcp URL and Authorization: Bearer <contact-specific token>. Do not append /mcp again or substitute the phone access token or a service-role key. Keep tokens in private service settings, not in chat. State clearly if the platform does not support this transport or long-running tool waits.\n\n2. Available tools\nUse tools/list as the authority for parameters and required fields:\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): call the phone. A contact-specific token already selects the identity, so contact_id may be omitted; other credentials must follow the tool schema.\n• tincall_current(): returns {call:object or null}; only reads the current call and does not start or wake an AI.\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?): waits for unanswered input and returns a matching input and job.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?): submits a reply; a complete reply waits for the next turn by default.\n• tincall_inputs(call_id): retrieves saved user inputs and the current reply job; deduplicate by message ID.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): ends the current call.\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?): lists calls for the current identity, newest first. limit defaults to 10 and ranges from 1 to 50.\n• tincall_record(call_id): reads text, saved images, and an optional summary submitted to this connector. No audio is returned. The summary may be empty when disabled, still generating, or failed.\n\n3. Obtain a real call and input\nCall tincall_current first. For an existing call, use its call.id. call:null means there is no current call; do not invent a call_id to wait on. Only when the user asks you to call them, generate new UUIDs for request_id and call_id and invoke tincall_call. Once it returns ringing, use that call.id with tincall_wait_for_input to wait for the phone to answer and for user input. Background delivery also requires push setup on the phone.\n\nFor a call started on the phone, the platform must keep the AI running or have a working wake bridge. After the phone starts the call, use tincall_current to obtain call.id, then wait for input. There is no tool to wait for an incoming call without a call_id. Copying a configuration or calling current does not wake an AI platform.\n\nRetain and follow voice_instructions whenever a wait result includes it, including speech expression requirements. It may be returned only once, even in a result with timed_out:true and input:null. Its absence in later results does not cancel those requirements. Reply only after receiving a non-null input and its matching job; do not invent a user message or an opening-turn job.\n\nTool data is provided in structuredContent or JSON text in content. Images are returned separately as standard MCP image content, preceded by text identifying message_id, image_id, and image_index. Do not rely only on image references in structured data. An image-only input can have empty text; still process its images and matching job.\n\n4. Reply and continue\nGenerate a new request_id for every new submission. Use the current call.id, job.reply_id, and job.epoch. For a complete reply, put the full text in text and set complete:true. When streaming, complete:false sends only the new fragment. The final complete:true must contain the full reply with all previously sent text as its prefix; never rewrite that prefix. The phone handles recognition, synthesis, and playback.\n\ncomplete:true accepts the reply and waits for the next turn by default. If its result already contains input and job, handle that turn directly without waiting again first. wait_for_input:false disables waiting after this submission. A wait defaults to, and cannot exceed, 120 seconds; timeout_seconds ranges from 1 to 120. timed_out:true is not a hangup. Continue with tincall_wait_for_input using the returned after_sequence.\n\nreply_accepted:true with wait_error means the reply was accepted but the subsequent wait failed. Continue using after_sequence without resending accepted text. If a network response is lost, retry with the original request_id and exactly the same parameters. For isError:true, read error.code. stale_epoch means the old job is no longer valid: read the current call and job rather than resending with an old job or epoch.\n\nStop when call.status is ended. Before hanging up, read the latest call state and invoke tincall_end with a new request_id, the existing call.id, and the latest call.epoch. Input, interruption, and hangup can change epoch; do not keep using its initial value. Acceptance of a reply does not mean playback has finished. After the call, use tincall_recent_calls to locate it and tincall_record to read its record and summary.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Cloud Sync & Calls → Connect to Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. End the call’s context when call.ended is received or call.status is confirmed as ended. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "下面说明如何让 AI 通过 Tincall 通话。MCP 用于支持 MCP 工具的 AI 平台；后端接法用于自行实现通话接口的服务。按实际接法执行，不要把普通模型 API 地址当成 Tincall 后端地址。\n\nMCP 接法\n\n一、在 AI 平台配置服务\n先在 Tincall「设置 → 连接云端」部署或连接支持 MCP 的服务，再编辑联系人，通话方式选 MCP、选择连接并保存。在保存后显示的配置页复制完整 MCP 配置；以后可在联系人编辑页点「查看并复制 MCP 配置」。将其导入对应 AI 平台的 MCP 服务设置，传输使用 Streamable HTTP，并检查工具列表。配置包含完整 /mcp 地址及 Authorization: Bearer <联系人专用令牌>，不要重复追加 /mcp，不要用手机访问令牌或 service-role 密钥替代。令牌只放私密服务配置，不贴进聊天。平台不支持该传输或长时间工具等待时，应明确说明。\n\n二、可用工具\n参数及必填项以 tools/list 为准：\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?)：向手机发起来电。联系人专用令牌已选择身份，可省略 contact_id；其他身份按工具要求填写。\n• tincall_current()：返回 {call:对象或null}，只查看当前电话，不启动或唤醒 AI。\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?)：等待未回复输入，返回匹配的 input 和 job。\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?)：提交回复，完整回复默认继续等待下一轮。\n• tincall_inputs(call_id)：补取已保存的用户输入及当前回复任务，按消息 ID 去重。\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch)：结束当前电话。\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?)：按新到旧列出当前身份的通话，limit 默认 10，范围 1–50。\n• tincall_record(call_id)：读取已提交到该连接端的通话文字、图片及可选摘要，不返回音频。摘要关闭、生成中或失败时可能为空。\n\n三、取得真实通话和输入\n先调用 tincall_current。已有电话时使用返回的 call.id；call:null 表示当前没有电话，不能编造 call_id 去等待。用户要求你主动打来时，才生成新的 UUID 作为 request_id 和 call_id 调用 tincall_call；返回 ringing 后即可用该 call.id 调用 tincall_wait_for_input，等待手机接听及用户输入。后台送达还需要手机完成推送配置。\n\n用户从手机拨号时，平台须保持 AI 运行，或已接好真实的唤醒桥；手机开始电话后用 tincall_current 取得 call.id，再等待输入。当前没有不带 call_id 的“等待来电”工具，复制配置或调用 current 也不会自动唤醒 AI 平台。\n\n等待结果中如有 voice_instructions，应立即保留并遵循，包括其中的语音表达要求。它可能只随首次等待返回，即使该次 timed_out:true、input:null 也可能出现；后续字段缺席不代表要求失效。只有拿到非空 input 和匹配的 job 后才回复，不虚构用户发言或首句任务。\n\n工具数据在 structuredContent 或 content 中的 JSON 文本里。图片另以标准 MCP image content 返回，前面的文本给出 message_id、image_id、image_index；不能只读结构化数据中的图片引用。仅图片输入的 text 可以为空，仍需结合图片及匹配任务回复。\n\n四、提交回复并继续通话\n每次新提交生成新的 request_id，使用当前 call.id、job.reply_id 和 job.epoch。完整回复放 text，设 complete:true；如先流式发送，complete:false 的 text 只放本次新增片段，最后 complete:true 必须提交包含已发送前缀的完整正文，不改写前缀。手机负责语音识别、合成及播放。\n\ncomplete:true 默认接受文字后继续等待下一轮。返回中已有 input 和 job 时，直接处理该轮，不再先调用等待。wait_for_input:false 可关闭这次提交后的等待。单次等待默认且最多 120 秒，timeout_seconds 范围 1–120；timed_out:true 不等于挂断，用返回的 after_sequence 调用 tincall_wait_for_input 续等。\n\nreply_accepted:true 且含 wait_error 表示回复已接受、后续等待失败；保留 after_sequence 续等，不重发已接受的文字。网络响应丢失时，重试复用原 request_id 和完全相同的参数。遇到 isError:true 先读取 error.code；stale_epoch 表示旧任务已失效，应重新读取当前电话和任务，不用旧 job 或 epoch 重发。\n\ncall.status 为 ended 时停止。主动挂断前读取最新通话状态，用新的 request_id、已有 call.id 和最新 call.epoch 调用 tincall_end。输入、打断和挂断都可能改变 epoch，不能一直沿用初始值。工具接受回复不表示手机已播完。结束后可用 tincall_recent_calls 找到通话，再用 tincall_record 读取记录与摘要。\n\n后端接法\n\n一、连接与基础格式\n自有后端负责人物设定、上下文和真实生成，手机负责收音、识别、朗读和本地记录。后端实现下面的 HTTPS / JSON 通话接口，无需实现 MCP，也不必开启云端备份。手机在「连接云端 → 连接已有服务」保存 HTTPS 基础地址和手机访问令牌、检查连接，再到联系人编辑页选择后端、该连接及对话对象。\n\n以下路径相对于基础地址。手机发送 Authorization: Bearer <手机访问令牌>，JSON 请求带 Content-Type: application/json 和 Accept: application/json；成功响应为 HTTP 200 的 JSON，不依赖重定向。错误返回非成功 HTTP 状态及 {error:{code:\"错误代码\"}}。写请求按 request_id 去重，相同请求重试返回原结果；同一 ID 不能更改内容。隔离不同访问身份的数据，不让客户端自行声明所有者。\n\ncall 对象必须包含 id(UUID)、contact_id(字符串)、source(\"backend\")、status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\")、epoch(非负整数)、last_sequence(非负整数)。一个 call_id 对应一通电话，message_id 对应一条输入，reply_id 对应一轮回复，不可混用。\n\n二、发现、开始和接听\nGET /capabilities 返回 {bindings:[{contact_id:\"联系人标识\",display_name:\"显示名\",generation_configured:true}]}；display_name 可省略，只有标识非空且 generation_configured:true 的对象才可在手机选择。\n\nPOST /calls 接收 request_id、call_id、contact_id、source:\"backend\"、expression_prompt，返回 {call}；新通话为 active、epoch:0，并产生 call.started 事件。GET /calls/current 返回 {call:对象或null}。如支持后端主动来电，已有 ringing 通话由 POST /calls/{call_id}/answer 接收 request_id、epoch、expression_prompt，返回 active 的 {call}，产生 call.started。expression_prompt 为语音表达要求，可为空；后端负责将其用于生成。\n\n三、输入与回复事件\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input 接收 request_id、message_id、当前 epoch、text，以及可选 images。每张图片为 {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg或image/png\",data_base64:\"标准Base64\"}，最多四张、每张最多 5 MiB，Base64 不带 data URI 前缀。有图时 text 可为空，无图时文字须非空。返回 {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}：input_id 等于 message_id，epoch 已递增一次。保存输入，取消旧生成，并产生 input.accepted、reply.started 后启动本轮生成。\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 返回 {call,events,cursor,has_more}。事件结构为 {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}，sequence 从 1 连续递增。after 默认 0，后续使用上次 cursor；已有事件立即返回，没有则等待新事件或到期返回 events:[]、cursor:N、has_more:false。空页不是挂断；has_more:true 时手机立即续取，不因 call 快照已结束而漏掉尾页。\n\ninput.accepted 和 reply.started 的 payload 包含 input_id、reply_id。reply.delta 另带 delta(新增片段)；reply.completed 另带 text(最终全文，包含已发前缀)；reply.failed 另带 code；reply.interrupted 另带 reason。这些事件的通话、输入、回复和 epoch 必须匹配；手机只接收当前代次，旧结果不得覆盖已保存内容。\n\n四、打断与挂断\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"interrupted\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回保持 active 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.interrupted。POST /calls/{call_id}/end 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"hangup\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回 ended 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.ended。保留已收到文字与中断原因，拒绝旧代次写入；过期代次用 stale_epoch 错误说明。\n\nreply.completed 只结束一句回复，只有挂断才结束这通电话的上下文。若要在挂断后将摘要写回其他对话，应由后端的通话结束流程实现并去重，不能把每句完成、空事件页或网络超时当作挂断。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tool support, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. Follow the approach you actually use. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Configure the service in the AI platform\nIn Tincall, deploy or connect an MCP-capable service under Settings → Connect to Cloud. Edit a contact, choose MCP and the connection, then save. Copy the complete MCP configuration from the screen shown after saving; later, use View and Copy MCP Configuration in the contact editor. Import it into the matching AI platform’s MCP service settings, use Streamable HTTP, and check the tool list. The configuration contains the full /mcp URL and Authorization: Bearer <contact-specific token>. Do not append /mcp again or substitute the phone access token or a service-role key. Keep tokens in private service settings, not in chat. State clearly if the platform does not support this transport or long-running tool waits.\n\n2. Available tools\nUse tools/list as the authority for parameters and required fields:\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): call the phone. A contact-specific token already selects the identity, so contact_id may be omitted; other credentials must follow the tool schema.\n• tincall_current(): returns {call:object or null}; only reads the current call and does not start or wake an AI.\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?): waits for unanswered input and returns a matching input and job.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?): submits a reply; a complete reply waits for the next turn by default.\n• tincall_inputs(call_id): retrieves saved user inputs and the current reply job; deduplicate by message ID.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): ends the current call.\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?): lists calls for the current identity, newest first. limit defaults to 10 and ranges from 1 to 50.\n• tincall_record(call_id): reads text, saved images, and an optional summary submitted to this connector. No audio is returned. The summary may be empty when disabled, still generating, or failed.\n\n3. Obtain a real call and input\nCall tincall_current first. For an existing call, use its call.id. call:null means there is no current call; do not invent a call_id to wait on. Only when the user asks you to call them, generate new UUIDs for request_id and call_id and invoke tincall_call. Once it returns ringing, use that call.id with tincall_wait_for_input to wait for the phone to answer and for user input. Background delivery also requires push setup on the phone.\n\nFor a call started on the phone, the platform must keep the AI running or have a working wake bridge. After the phone starts the call, use tincall_current to obtain call.id, then wait for input. There is no tool to wait for an incoming call without a call_id. Copying a configuration or calling current does not wake an AI platform.\n\nRetain and follow voice_instructions whenever a wait result includes it, including speech expression requirements. It may be returned only once, even in a result with timed_out:true and input:null. Its absence in later results does not cancel those requirements. Reply only after receiving a non-null input and its matching job; do not invent a user message or an opening-turn job.\n\nTool data is provided in structuredContent or JSON text in content. Images are returned separately as standard MCP image content, preceded by text identifying message_id, image_id, and image_index. Do not rely only on image references in structured data. An image-only input can have empty text; still process its images and matching job.\n\n4. Reply and continue\nGenerate a new request_id for every new submission. Use the current call.id, job.reply_id, and job.epoch. For a complete reply, put the full text in text and set complete:true. When streaming, complete:false sends only the new fragment. The final complete:true must contain the full reply with all previously sent text as its prefix; never rewrite that prefix. The phone handles recognition, synthesis, and playback.\n\ncomplete:true accepts the reply and waits for the next turn by default. If its result already contains input and job, handle that turn directly without waiting again first. wait_for_input:false disables waiting after this submission. A wait defaults to, and cannot exceed, 120 seconds; timeout_seconds ranges from 1 to 120. timed_out:true is not a hangup. Continue with tincall_wait_for_input using the returned after_sequence.\n\nreply_accepted:true with wait_error means the reply was accepted but the subsequent wait failed. Continue using after_sequence without resending accepted text. If a network response is lost, retry with the original request_id and exactly the same parameters. For isError:true, read error.code. stale_epoch means the old job is no longer valid: read the current call and job rather than resending with an old job or epoch.\n\nStop when call.status is ended. Before hanging up, read the latest call state and invoke tincall_end with a new request_id, the existing call.id, and the latest call.epoch. Input, interruption, and hangup can change epoch; do not keep using its initial value. Acceptance of a reply does not mean playback has finished. After the call, use tincall_recent_calls to locate it and tincall_record to read its record and summary.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Connect to Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. A hangup ends the call’s context. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "下面说明如何让 AI 通过 Tincall 通话。MCP 用于支持 MCP 工具的 AI 平台；后端接法用于自行实现通话接口的服务。按实际接法执行，不要把普通模型 API 地址当成 Tincall 后端地址。\n\nMCP 接法\n\n一、在 AI 平台配置服务\n先在 Tincall「设置 → 连接云端」部署或连接支持 MCP 的服务，再编辑联系人，通话方式选 MCP、选择连接并保存。在保存后显示的配置页复制完整 MCP 配置；以后可在联系人编辑页点「查看并复制 MCP 配置」。将其导入对应 AI 平台的 MCP 服务设置，传输使用 Streamable HTTP，并检查工具列表。配置包含完整 /mcp 地址及 Authorization: Bearer <联系人专用令牌>，不要重复追加 /mcp，不要用手机访问令牌或 service-role 密钥替代。令牌只放私密服务配置，不贴进聊天。平台不支持该传输或长时间工具等待时，应明确说明。\n\n二、可用工具\n参数及必填项以 tools/list 为准：\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?)：向手机发起来电。联系人专用令牌已选择身份，可省略 contact_id；其他身份按工具要求填写。\n• tincall_current()：返回 {call:对象或null}，只查看当前电话，不启动或唤醒 AI。\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?)：等待未回复输入，返回匹配的 input 和 job。\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?)：提交回复，完整回复默认继续等待下一轮。\n• tincall_inputs(call_id)：补取已保存的用户输入及当前回复任务，按消息 ID 去重。\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch)：结束当前电话。\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?)：按新到旧列出当前身份的通话，limit 默认 10，范围 1–50。\n• tincall_record(call_id)：读取已提交到该连接端的通话文字、图片及可选摘要，不返回音频。摘要关闭、生成中或失败时可能为空。\n\n三、取得真实通话和输入\n先调用 tincall_current。已有电话时使用返回的 call.id；call:null 表示当前没有电话，不能编造 call_id 去等待。用户要求你主动打来时，才生成新的 UUID 作为 request_id 和 call_id 调用 tincall_call；返回 ringing 后即可用该 call.id 调用 tincall_wait_for_input，等待手机接听及用户输入。后台送达还需要手机完成推送配置。\n\n用户从手机拨号时，平台须保持 AI 运行，或已接好真实的唤醒桥；手机开始电话后用 tincall_current 取得 call.id，再等待输入。当前没有不带 call_id 的“等待来电”工具，复制配置或调用 current 也不会自动唤醒 AI 平台。\n\n等待结果中如有 voice_instructions，应立即保留并遵循，包括其中的语音表达要求。它可能只随首次等待返回，即使该次 timed_out:true、input:null 也可能出现；后续字段缺席不代表要求失效。只有拿到非空 input 和匹配的 job 后才回复，不虚构用户发言或首句任务。\n\n工具数据在 structuredContent 或 content 中的 JSON 文本里。图片另以标准 MCP image content 返回，前面的文本给出 message_id、image_id、image_index；不能只读结构化数据中的图片引用。仅图片输入的 text 可以为空，仍需结合图片及匹配任务回复。\n\n四、提交回复并继续通话\n每次新提交生成新的 request_id，使用当前 call.id、job.reply_id 和 job.epoch。完整回复放 text，设 complete:true；如先流式发送，complete:false 的 text 只放本次新增片段，最后 complete:true 必须提交包含已发送前缀的完整正文，不改写前缀。手机负责语音识别、合成及播放。\n\ncomplete:true 默认接受文字后继续等待下一轮。返回中已有 input 和 job 时，直接处理该轮，不再先调用等待。wait_for_input:false 可关闭这次提交后的等待。单次等待默认且最多 120 秒，timeout_seconds 范围 1–120；timed_out:true 不等于挂断，用返回的 after_sequence 调用 tincall_wait_for_input 续等。\n\nreply_accepted:true 且含 wait_error 表示回复已接受、后续等待失败；保留 after_sequence 续等，不重发已接受的文字。网络响应丢失时，重试复用原 request_id 和完全相同的参数。遇到 isError:true 先读取 error.code；stale_epoch 表示旧任务已失效，应重新读取当前电话和任务，不用旧 job 或 epoch 重发。\n\ncall.status 为 ended 时停止。主动挂断前读取最新通话状态，用新的 request_id、已有 call.id 和最新 call.epoch 调用 tincall_end。输入、打断和挂断都可能改变 epoch，不能一直沿用初始值。工具接受回复不表示手机已播完。结束后可用 tincall_recent_calls 找到通话，再用 tincall_record 读取记录与摘要。\n\n后端接法\n\n一、连接与基础格式\n自有后端负责人物设定、上下文和真实生成，手机负责收音、识别、朗读和本地记录。后端实现下面的 HTTPS / JSON 通话接口，无需实现 MCP，也不必开启云端备份。手机在「连接云端 → 连接已有服务」保存 HTTPS 基础地址和手机访问令牌、检查连接，再到联系人编辑页选择后端、该连接及对话对象。\n\n以下路径相对于基础地址。手机发送 Authorization: Bearer <手机访问令牌>，JSON 请求带 Content-Type: application/json 和 Accept: application/json；成功响应为 HTTP 200 的 JSON，不依赖重定向。错误返回非成功 HTTP 状态及 {error:{code:\"错误代码\"}}。写请求按 request_id 去重，相同请求重试返回原结果；同一 ID 不能更改内容。隔离不同访问身份的数据，不让客户端自行声明所有者。\n\ncall 对象必须包含 id(UUID)、contact_id(字符串)、source(\"backend\")、status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\")、epoch(非负整数)、last_sequence(非负整数)。一个 call_id 对应一通电话，message_id 对应一条输入，reply_id 对应一轮回复，不可混用。\n\n二、发现、开始和接听\nGET /capabilities 返回 {bindings:[{contact_id:\"联系人标识\",display_name:\"显示名\",generation_configured:true}]}；display_name 可省略，只有标识非空且 generation_configured:true 的对象才可在手机选择。\n\nPOST /calls 接收 request_id、call_id、contact_id、source:\"backend\"、expression_prompt，返回 {call}；新通话为 active、epoch:0，并产生 call.started 事件。GET /calls/current 返回 {call:对象或null}。如支持后端主动来电，已有 ringing 通话由 POST /calls/{call_id}/answer 接收 request_id、epoch、expression_prompt，返回 active 的 {call}，产生 call.started。expression_prompt 为语音表达要求，可为空；后端负责将其用于生成。\n\n三、输入与回复事件\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input 接收 request_id、message_id、当前 epoch、text，以及可选 images。每张图片为 {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg或image/png\",data_base64:\"标准Base64\"}，最多四张、每张最多 5 MiB，Base64 不带 data URI 前缀。有图时 text 可为空，无图时文字须非空。返回 {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}：input_id 等于 message_id，epoch 已递增一次。保存输入，取消旧生成，并产生 input.accepted、reply.started 后启动本轮生成。\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 返回 {call,events,cursor,has_more}。事件结构为 {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}，sequence 从 1 连续递增。after 默认 0，后续使用上次 cursor；已有事件立即返回，没有则等待新事件或到期返回 events:[]、cursor:N、has_more:false。空页不是挂断；has_more:true 时手机立即续取，不因 call 快照已结束而漏掉尾页。\n\ninput.accepted 和 reply.started 的 payload 包含 input_id、reply_id。reply.delta 另带 delta(新增片段)；reply.completed 另带 text(最终全文，包含已发前缀)；reply.failed 另带 code；reply.interrupted 另带 reason。这些事件的通话、输入、回复和 epoch 必须匹配；手机只接收当前代次，旧结果不得覆盖已保存内容。\n\n四、打断与挂断\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"interrupted\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回保持 active 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.interrupted。POST /calls/{call_id}/end 接收 request_id、epoch、reason:\"hangup\"，取消生成、递增 epoch，返回 ended 的 {call}；有未完成回复先产生 reply.interrupted，再产生 call.ended。保留已收到文字与中断原因，拒绝旧代次写入；过期代次用 stale_epoch 错误说明。\n\nreply.completed 只结束一句回复。收到 call.ended 或确认 call.status 为 ended 时，结束这通电话的上下文。若要在挂断后将摘要写回其他对话，应由后端的通话结束流程实现并去重，不能把每句完成、空事件页或网络超时当作挂断。" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "These instructions explain how an AI can make calls through Tincall. Use MCP for an AI platform with MCP tool support, or the backend approach for a service implementing the call API. Follow the approach you actually use. A regular model API endpoint is not a Tincall backend endpoint.\n\nMCP integration\n\n1. Configure the service in the AI platform\nIn Tincall, deploy or connect an MCP-capable service under Settings → Connect to Cloud. Edit a contact, choose MCP and the connection, then save. Copy the complete MCP configuration from the screen shown after saving; later, use View and Copy MCP Configuration in the contact editor. Import it into the matching AI platform’s MCP service settings, use Streamable HTTP, and check the tool list. The configuration contains the full /mcp URL and Authorization: Bearer <contact-specific token>. Do not append /mcp again or substitute the phone access token or a service-role key. Keep tokens in private service settings, not in chat. State clearly if the platform does not support this transport or long-running tool waits.\n\n2. Available tools\nUse tools/list as the authority for parameters and required fields:\n• tincall_call(request_id, call_id, contact_id?): call the phone. A contact-specific token already selects the identity, so contact_id may be omitted; other credentials must follow the tool schema.\n• tincall_current(): returns {call:object or null}; only reads the current call and does not start or wake an AI.\n• tincall_wait_for_input(call_id, after_sequence?, timeout_seconds?): waits for unanswered input and returns a matching input and job.\n• tincall_reply(request_id, call_id, reply_id, epoch, text, complete, wait_for_input?, timeout_seconds?): submits a reply; a complete reply waits for the next turn by default.\n• tincall_inputs(call_id): retrieves saved user inputs and the current reply job; deduplicate by message ID.\n• tincall_end(request_id, call_id, epoch): ends the current call.\n• tincall_recent_calls(limit?): lists calls for the current identity, newest first. limit defaults to 10 and ranges from 1 to 50.\n• tincall_record(call_id): reads text, saved images, and an optional summary submitted to this connector. No audio is returned. The summary may be empty when disabled, still generating, or failed.\n\n3. Obtain a real call and input\nCall tincall_current first. For an existing call, use its call.id. call:null means there is no current call; do not invent a call_id to wait on. Only when the user asks you to call them, generate new UUIDs for request_id and call_id and invoke tincall_call. Once it returns ringing, use that call.id with tincall_wait_for_input to wait for the phone to answer and for user input. Background delivery also requires push setup on the phone.\n\nFor a call started on the phone, the platform must keep the AI running or have a working wake bridge. After the phone starts the call, use tincall_current to obtain call.id, then wait for input. There is no tool to wait for an incoming call without a call_id. Copying a configuration or calling current does not wake an AI platform.\n\nRetain and follow voice_instructions whenever a wait result includes it, including speech expression requirements. It may be returned only once, even in a result with timed_out:true and input:null. Its absence in later results does not cancel those requirements. Reply only after receiving a non-null input and its matching job; do not invent a user message or an opening-turn job.\n\nTool data is provided in structuredContent or JSON text in content. Images are returned separately as standard MCP image content, preceded by text identifying message_id, image_id, and image_index. Do not rely only on image references in structured data. An image-only input can have empty text; still process its images and matching job.\n\n4. Reply and continue\nGenerate a new request_id for every new submission. Use the current call.id, job.reply_id, and job.epoch. For a complete reply, put the full text in text and set complete:true. When streaming, complete:false sends only the new fragment. The final complete:true must contain the full reply with all previously sent text as its prefix; never rewrite that prefix. The phone handles recognition, synthesis, and playback.\n\ncomplete:true accepts the reply and waits for the next turn by default. If its result already contains input and job, handle that turn directly without waiting again first. wait_for_input:false disables waiting after this submission. A wait defaults to, and cannot exceed, 120 seconds; timeout_seconds ranges from 1 to 120. timed_out:true is not a hangup. Continue with tincall_wait_for_input using the returned after_sequence.\n\nreply_accepted:true with wait_error means the reply was accepted but the subsequent wait failed. Continue using after_sequence without resending accepted text. If a network response is lost, retry with the original request_id and exactly the same parameters. For isError:true, read error.code. stale_epoch means the old job is no longer valid: read the current call and job rather than resending with an old job or epoch.\n\nStop when call.status is ended. Before hanging up, read the latest call state and invoke tincall_end with a new request_id, the existing call.id, and the latest call.epoch. Input, interruption, and hangup can change epoch; do not keep using its initial value. Acceptance of a reply does not mean playback has finished. After the call, use tincall_recent_calls to locate it and tincall_record to read its record and summary.\n\nBackend integration\n\n1. Connection and base format\nA custom backend manages persona, context, and real generation. The phone handles capture, recognition, speech playback, and local records. Implement the HTTPS / JSON call endpoints below; MCP and cloud backups are not required. On the phone, save an HTTPS base URL and phone access token under Connect to Cloud → Connect an Existing Service and check the connection. Then choose Backend, that connection, and a conversation partner in the contact editor.\n\nAll paths below are relative to the base URL. The phone sends Authorization: Bearer <phone access token>. JSON requests use Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json. Successful responses are HTTP 200 JSON; do not depend on redirects. Errors use a non-success HTTP status and {error:{code:\"error_code\"}}. Deduplicate writes by request_id: an identical retry returns the original result; the same ID must not be reused with different content. Isolate data by authenticated identity rather than accepting a client-declared owner.\n\nA call object must contain id(UUID), contact_id(string), source(\"backend\"), status(\"active\"/\"ringing\"/\"ended\"), epoch(non-negative integer), and last_sequence(non-negative integer). A call_id identifies one call, message_id one input, and reply_id one reply turn. Do not interchange them.\n\n2. Discovery, starting, and answering\nGET /capabilities returns {bindings:[{contact_id:\"character_id\",display_name:\"Display name\",generation_configured:true}]}. display_name is optional. The phone only offers entries with a non-empty identifier and generation_configured:true.\n\nPOST /calls accepts request_id, call_id, contact_id, source:\"backend\", and expression_prompt, and returns {call}. A new call is active with epoch:0 and emits call.started. GET /calls/current returns {call:object or null}. If the backend supports incoming calls, POST /calls/{call_id}/answer accepts request_id, epoch, and expression_prompt for an existing ringing call, returns an active {call}, and emits call.started. expression_prompt contains speech expression requirements and may be empty; the backend is responsible for applying it during generation.\n\n3. Input and reply events\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/input accepts request_id, message_id, the current epoch, text, and optional images. Each image is {id:\"UUID\",mime_type:\"image/jpeg or image/png\",data_base64:\"standard Base64\"}. Up to four images are allowed, each at most 5 MiB; Base64 has no data URI prefix. text may be empty with images but must be non-empty without them. Return {call,input_id,reply_id,epoch}: input_id equals message_id and epoch has incremented once. Save the input, cancel any old generation, emit input.accepted and reply.started, and start this turn’s generation.\n\nGET /calls/{call_id}/events?after=N&limit=100&wait=20 returns {call,events,cursor,has_more}. Each event is {sequence,call_id,epoch,type,payload}; sequence increases consecutively from 1. after defaults to 0; subsequent requests use the previous cursor. Return existing events immediately, otherwise wait for new events or return events:[], cursor:N, has_more:false on timeout. An empty page is not a hangup. With has_more:true, the phone fetches the next page immediately, including remaining events when the call snapshot is already ended.\n\ninput.accepted and reply.started carry input_id and reply_id in payload. reply.delta also carries delta(new text); reply.completed carries text(the final full reply including its previously sent prefix); reply.failed carries code; reply.interrupted carries reason. Call, input, reply, and epoch must match. The phone accepts only the current epoch; old results must not overwrite saved content.\n\n4. Interruption and hangup\nPOST /calls/{call_id}/interrupt accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"interrupted\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an active {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.interrupted. POST /calls/{call_id}/end accepts request_id, epoch, and reason:\"hangup\". Cancel generation, increment epoch, and return an ended {call}. Emit reply.interrupted for an unfinished reply, then call.ended. Preserve received text and interruption reasons, reject old-epoch writes, and use stale_epoch for an outdated epoch.\n\nreply.completed ends only one reply. End the call’s context when call.ended is received or call.status is confirmed as ended. If summaries should be written back into another conversation after hangup, implement and deduplicate that work in the backend’s call-end flow. Do not treat each completed reply, an empty event page, or a network timeout as a hangup."
          }
        }
      }
    },
